angles between 50 and 90◦ and must be abandoned for lesser angles.” Also, in 1781, Leonhard Euler (1707–1783) pointed out the physical inconsistency of Newton’s model (Figure 1.7) consisting of a rectilinear stream of particles impacting without warning on a surface. In contrast to this


